# Puck Firmware — ESP32-C3 LED Puck
# File: src/puck/main.cpp
# FW_VERSION: 87

## PURPOSE
Standalone firmware for the ESP32-C3 LED pucks. Handles LED animations, button input,
sound sequences, ESP-NOW communication with the coordinator, battery monitoring,
and temperature protection.

## HARDWARE
- MCU: ESP32-C3 (Single-Core RISC-V)
- 35x WS2812B LEDs (PIN 4, GRB order)
- Piezo Buzzer (PIN 5)
- Arcade Button (PIN 3, INPUT_PULLUP)
- Battery ADC (PIN 0, voltage divider 2:1)
- NTC Temp Sensor (PIN 6, 10k Beta3950, optional — DISABLE_TEMP_SENSOR flag)
- FastLED power limit: 5V / 1500mA

## BOOT SEQUENCE
1. Buzzer off (safety after WDT reset)
2. ADC + Button + FastLED init
3. Battery boot check: <3400mV → low battery lockout, <3700mV → battery save mode
4. Mario startup sound
5. Watchdog: 3s timeout, panic on hang
6. WiFi STA mode, ESP-NOW init on WIFI_CHANNEL
7. Promiscuous sniffer registered but disabled by default (CPU savings)
8. Broadcast peer added

## MAIN LOOP (loop())
1. Watchdog reset
2. OTA check
3. Process incoming command queue (ISR → ringbuffer → main loop)
4. Button handling (debounce + glitch filter)
5. runAnimation() — LED frame rendering with 15 FPS cap
6. runSound() — non-blocking sound sequence engine
7. Battery check (every 2s, 5-sample rolling average)
8. Temperature check (every 2s, overheat protection at 60°C)
9. Coordinator disconnect detection (15s timeout)
10. Heartbeat sending (timing-offset from LED refresh)

## LED TIMING (Anti-Flicker, v87)
Problem: On the single-core ESP32-C3, FastLED.show() and ESP-NOW traffic can collide,
causing WS2812B timing glitches (visible as LED flicker).

Solution (3 measures):
- **15 FPS Cap**: LED_MIN_FRAME_MS = 67ms — no effect runs faster than 15 FPS,
  regardless of anim.speed setting. Reduces collision windows.
- **yield() after show()**: Immediately after FastLED.show(), yield() gives the WiFi
  stack a chance to process pending ESP-NOW packets.
- **Heartbeat offset**: Outgoing heartbeats (EVT_HELLO/EVT_HEARTBEAT) are only sent
  when at least HEARTBEAT_OFFSET_MS (30ms) have passed since the last FastLED.show().
  This places ESP-NOW transmissions in the middle of the frame gap, away from LED updates.

Constants:
- LED_MIN_FRAME_MS = 67 (~15 FPS max)
- LED_GUARD_MS = 5 (minimum gap after show before any TX)
- HEARTBEAT_OFFSET_MS = 30 (preferred TX point in frame gap)
- lastShowTime: global timestamp of last FastLED.show()

## ANIMATION ENGINE (runAnimation())
- Frame rate: max(anim.speed, LED_MIN_FRAME_MS), except EFF_PROGRESS (immediate)
- EFF_FLASH_BEEP: one-shot, times out after anim.speed ms
- All effects write to leds[] array, then FastLED.show() + yield()
- Supports: OFF, STATIC, BLINK, FLASH, BLINK_COUNT, STATUS, PROGRESS, BREATHE,
  BREATHE_MOD2, BREATHE_MOD4, SINGLE_CHASE, DOUBLE_CHASE, SPLIT_ROT, RAINBOW,
  COUNTDOWN, LOADING, WIN, FAIL, SPARKLE, POLICE

## SOUND ENGINE (runSound())
- Non-blocking note sequencer with Note array (freq + duration)
- Special mode: isExplosion (random frequencies 50-400Hz)
- Sequences: OFF, FANFARE, ERROR, EXPLOSION, HERO, MARIO, TETRIS, RACE, SKI, DINGDONG

## ESP-NOW COMMUNICATION
- Receive: ISR callback → cmdQueue[10] ringbuffer (portMUX spinlock protected)
- Send: sendEvent() — 3x retransmit with 5ms delay for reliability
- Deduplication: globalSeqCounter (TX), lastReceivedSeq (RX)

### Pairing Flow
1. Unpaired: send EVT_HELLO every 2s (broadcast)
2. Coordinator responds with CMD_PAIR_ACK → store coordinator MAC, isPaired = true
3. Paired: send EVT_HEARTBEAT every 5s
4. Disconnect: no command received for 15s → isPaired = false, red STATUS LED, re-pair

### Heartbeat (Bidirectional, v81+)
- Puck → Coordinator: EVT_HEARTBEAT every 5s (includes battery_mv, fw_version, temp_c10)
- Coordinator → Puck: CMD_KEEPALIVE every 10s
- Puck timeout: COORDINATOR_TIMEOUT_MS = 15s → disconnect + re-pair
- Heartbeat TX timing offset from LED refresh (v87, see LED TIMING section)

### Command Processing (processIncomingCommands())
- CMD_PING: force re-pair
- CMD_KEEPALIVE: bidirectional heartbeat (updates lastCommandFromCoordinator)
- CMD_PAIR_ACK: complete pairing, store coordinator MAC, enable promiscuous if STATUS
- CMD_EFFECT: setEffect() — LED animation with color, speed, brightness, sound
- CMD_SOUND / CMD_SEQUENCE: trigger sound sequence
- CMD_SET_BRIGHTNESS: global brightness limit (10-100%)

## BATTERY PROTECTION
- Boot check: 8 samples averaged
  - <3400mV (BAT_CRITICAL_MV): lockout mode, red countdown animation
  - <3700mV (BAT_LOW_BOOT_MV): battery save mode (50% brightness cap)
- Runtime: every 2s, 5-sample rolling average
  - <=3400mV: critical lockout with countdown animation
  - <=3600mV (BAT_WARNING_MV): battery save mode
  - <1000mV: no sensor detected, skip monitoring

## TEMPERATURE PROTECTION
- Check every 2s via NTC (Steinhart-Hart/Beta equation)
- >=60°C: overheat mode — LEDs off, aggressive beeping (250ms on/off) for 30s
- Recovery: temperature drops below 55°C (5°C hysteresis)
- DISABLE_TEMP_SENSOR define: skip for old pucks without NTC

## OTA UPDATE
- Triggered by CMD_UPDATE with SSID/password payload
- Connects to WiFi, fetches firmware from http://192.168.42.1/firmware.bin
- LED progress bar (purple → blue → green/red result)

## RSSI SNIFFER
- Promiscuous mode callback filters packets by coordinator MAC
- Only active during EFF_STATUS effect (saves CPU otherwise)
- Used for signal strength display (red if RSSI < -80)
